479785 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186479453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186479472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186479652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186479727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186479373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479785 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "85870cc2-890e-5529-ad2f-e4ee9e1292eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479826 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479826 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479826 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479826 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $‖u‖=5$ and $u\\cdot v=-30$, find the smallest possible value of $‖3v‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479826 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0502cc65-db2e-5570-9171-0d7053693770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479826 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-30| & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 6 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 6 & \\le 3\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 18 & \\le ‖3v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖3v‖$ is $18.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479875 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479875 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479875 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479875 #edb/ref 1071 "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479875 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9369c09e-6bcc-5680-9471-b4a602dad377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479875 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{140}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{35}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{35}})≈{75.31}^{∘}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479879 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479879 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479879 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479879 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A(4,-1,1,0)$, $B(4,2,1,-1)$, and $C(0,-5,3,2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479879 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9155dd9-42f9-5296-ab8b-8f9a62ed1901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479879 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{14}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{14÷2}{20÷2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479886 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479886 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74108" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479886 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479886 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A(2,2,1,-1)$ and $B(1,0,0,3).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479886 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b814c1fe-b3ea-5814-8155-d4d3b5c1b767" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479886 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
